        "original_id": "c19beff3-95b4-5963-91a4-9c5f6e43765f",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Vinessa Shaw, Stanley Kubrick, Wes Craven, Josh Hartnett, Arthur Schnitzler, Nicole Kidman, Tom Cruise\n- Works: Ladybugs, Eyes Wide Shut, The Hills Have Eyes, 40 Days and 40 Nights, Traumnovelle\n- Topics: Film roles, adaptations, filmography\n\nFacts:\n- Arthur Schnitzler wrote the 1926 novella Traumnovelle, also translated as Dream Story.\n- Eyes Wide Shut is based on Arthur Schnitzler's 1926 novella Traumnovelle.\n- Eyes Wide Shut transfers the story setting from early 20th century Vienna to 1990s New York City.\n- Vinessa Shaw appeared in the film Ladybugs in 1992.\n- Stanley Kubrick directed Eyes Wide Shut, which was released in 1999.\n- Nicole Kidman worked with Tom Cruise again in Stanley Kubrick's 1999 erotic thriller Eyes Wide Shut.\n- Vinessa Shaw appeared in Stanley Kubrick's 1999 film Eyes Wide Shut.\n- Vinessa Shaw played Josh Hartnett's character's sadistic ex-girlfriend in 40 Days and 40 Nights.\n- Vinessa Shaw appeared in the 2006 remake of Wes Craven's horror film The Hills Have Eyes.",
